feat(lpa-susceptibility): pre-register the Lp(a) by arterial-susceptibility test

Asks whether a non-lipid coronary polygenic score amplifies the effect of
Lp(a) as it does that of measured ApoB in the metabolome-resilience work.
PREREGISTRATION.md fixes, before any estimate is computed:

  primary    product of genetically predicted Lp(a) with the non-lipid
             score, in the cohort, outcome and full-quadratic model of
             that work's stage 11 (379,654 participants, 15,978 events)
  rule       five verdicts on the product and on r = b(M:N) / b(M) relative
             to the ApoB reference; three count as lead-grade
  secondary  lipid-region product, spline, statin-free, sexes, windows,
             measured Lp(a), the 167-variant LDL-C score, the additive
             scale, and one model holding ApoB and Lp(a) together
  gates      the thirteen emulation gates, recorded cohort and event
             counts, and reproduction of two earlier estimates to 1e-6

lpa_susceptibility.R reuses the agent6 libraries and lpa_horizon.R
unchanged (the SLURM wrapper checks their md5s) and loads the latter into
its own environment. Synthetic self-test: LS6 job 3602197, 16 checks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 


